---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | CreateLoom"
  description="Learn how CreateLoom collects and uses information through analytics, advertising, browser storage, contact requests and third-party services."
>
  <article class="legal container">

    <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p class="updated">
      Last updated: September 14, 2026
    </p>

    <p>
      CreateLoom ("CreateLoom", "we", "us", or "our") operates
      <strong>createloom.vercel.app</strong> and provides AI image prompts,
      creator resources, guides and related content.
    </p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains what information CreateLoom collects or
      processes when you visit or interact with the website, why that
      information is used, and the choices available to you.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>

    <p>
      CreateLoom does not require an account to browse the website, view
      AI prompts or read articles. We do not intentionally collect
      sensitive personal information through the website.
    </p>

    <p>
      Information may be provided directly by you when you voluntarily
      contact us or communicate with us. This can include your name,
      email address and the contents of your message, depending on what
      you choose to provide.
    </p>

    <p>
      CreateLoom also processes certain technical and usage information
      through third-party services described below, including analytics
      and advertising technologies.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Browser storage and saved prompts</h2>

    <p>
      CreateLoom uses browser local storage for certain site features and
      preferences. In particular, the website can store prompts that you
      save or favorite so that your selections remain available when you
      return using the same browser.
    </p>

    <p>
      This saved-prompt information is stored locally in your browser and
      is not, by itself, sent to CreateLoom's servers.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can remove locally stored CreateLoom data through your browser
      settings or by clearing the site's stored data.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Analytics</h2>

    <p>
      CreateLoom uses <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to understand how
      visitors use the website and to measure website traffic and
      performance.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google Analytics may process information such as pages viewed,
      interactions with the website, approximate geographic information,
      browser and device information, referral information and other
      technical or usage information. The information collected depends
      on Google's technology and the configuration used on CreateLoom.
    </p>

    <p>
      Analytics information is used to understand which content is useful,
      identify website performance issues and improve the CreateLoom
      experience. CreateLoom does not use Google Analytics to intentionally
      collect sensitive personal information.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google Analytics data retention for CreateLoom is configured for
      <strong>14 months</strong> for user-level and event-level data. After
      the applicable retention period, Google Analytics automatically
      deletes that data according to its retention settings. Aggregated
      reporting may remain available where it is not subject to the same
      retention controls.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>

    <p>
      CreateLoom itself does not require cookies for basic browsing of the
      prompt library or blog. However, third-party services used on the
      website, including Google Analytics and Google advertising services,
      may use cookies or similar technologies as part of their operation.
    </p>

    <p>
      These technologies can be used for purposes such as measuring
      traffic, understanding website usage, delivering advertisements,
      measuring advertising performance and, where permitted, personalizing
      advertising.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings.
      Some website features or third-party services may work differently
      when cookies or similar technologies are restricted.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Advertising</h2>

    <p>
      CreateLoom uses Google AdSense advertising technology on the website
      and may display advertisements when the advertising service is
      eligible and enabled for the relevant page and visitor.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google and its advertising partners may use cookies or similar
      technologies to serve, measure and improve advertisements. Depending
      on applicable settings, user choices and location, advertising may
      be personalized or non-personalized.
    </p>

    <p>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, may use information from a
      user's previous visits to this website or other websites to provide
      or measure advertising. Google states that publishers must disclose
      the use of advertising cookies in their privacy policies.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can manage Google's personalized advertising settings through
      <a
        href="https://adssettings.google.com/"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank"
      >
        Google Ads Settings
      </a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      CreateLoom also participates in Google's privacy and consent
      mechanisms where applicable. Visitors in regions where consent is
      legally required may be shown a consent message before certain
      advertising or related technologies are used.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Contact requests</h2>

    <p>
      If you contact CreateLoom, we use the information you provide to
      read, respond to and manage your request.
    </p>

    <p>
      We do not sell contact information submitted directly to us. We
      retain contact information only for as long as reasonably necessary
      to handle the request, maintain appropriate records and meet
      applicable legal obligations.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Third-party services and links</h2>

    <p>
      CreateLoom uses or links to third-party services, platforms and
      websites. These services operate under their own privacy policies
      and terms.
    </p>

    <p>
      Third-party services used by or linked from CreateLoom may include
      Google Analytics, Google AdSense and other external platforms
      associated with creator resources, social media, advertising or
      website functionality.
    </p>

    <p>
      CreateLoom does not control the privacy practices of third-party
      websites. We encourage visitors to review the privacy policies of
      those services before providing personal information or interacting
      with them.
    </p>

    <h2>8. How we use information</h2>

    <p>
      CreateLoom uses information for legitimate website and business
      purposes, including:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Providing and maintaining the website and its features.</li>
      <li>Remembering locally saved prompts and browser preferences.</li>
      <li>Understanding website traffic and improving content and performance.</li>
      <li>Responding to contact requests and other communications.</li>
      <li>Displaying, measuring and improving advertising where applicable.</li>
      <li>Protecting the website and addressing misuse or security issues.</li>
      <li>Complying with applicable legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Data sharing</h2>

    <p>
      CreateLoom does not sell personal information submitted directly to
      us. Information may be processed or shared with service providers
      when necessary to operate the website, provide analytics, deliver
      advertising, handle communications, protect the website or comply
      with legal requirements.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>California privacy notice:</strong> CreateLoom does not
      knowingly sell personal information for monetary consideration.
      Where applicable under California law, you may have the right to
      opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information for
      cross-context behavioral advertising. CreateLoom does not
      discriminate against users for exercising applicable privacy rights.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google may process information through Google Analytics and Google
      advertising services according to Google's own policies and the
      configuration of those services.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children's privacy</h2>

    <p>
      CreateLoom is intended for users who are <strong>13 years of age or
      older</strong>. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
      children under 13 through the website.
    </p>

    <p>
      If applicable law in your location requires a higher minimum age for
      online services or consent, that higher age requirement applies.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you believe that a child has provided personal information to
      CreateLoom, please contact us so that we can review the situation
      and take appropriate action.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Your choices and rights</h2>

    <p>
      Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights
      relating to personal information, including rights to access,
      correct, delete or restrict certain processing of your information.
      You may also have choices regarding cookies, analytics and
      personalized advertising.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can control browser cookies and locally stored website data
      through your browser settings. You can also manage Google's
      personalized advertising settings through
      <a
        href="https://adssettings.google.com/"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank"
      >
        Google Ads Settings
      </a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Where required by applicable law, CreateLoom and its relevant
      advertising partners provide mechanisms for managing or withdrawing
      consent.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Data security</h2>

    <p>
      We take reasonable measures appropriate to the nature of the website
      and the information we process to protect information against
      unauthorized access, misuse or disclosure.
    </p>

    <p>
      No method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is
      completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>

    <p>
      We update this Privacy Policy when our website, services, analytics,
      advertising practices or legal obligations materially change.
    </p>

    <p>
      When we make changes, we update the "Last updated" date shown at the
      beginning of this policy. The updated policy applies from the date
      it is published on the website.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Contact</h2>

    <p>
      If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how CreateLoom
      handles information, please contact us through the
      <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="notice">
      This Privacy Policy describes CreateLoom's current website practices
      and is intended to provide clear information about how the website
      handles data. It is not legal advice. If CreateLoom introduces
      additional data-processing features, payments, memberships,
      newsletters or other services, this policy will be reviewed and
      updated as appropriate.
    </p>

  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 850px;
    padding-top: 70px;
    padding-bottom: 100px;
  }

  .legal h1 {
    margin: 10px 0 8px;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    margin: 42px 0 13px;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    letter-spacing: -.02em;
  }

  .legal p,
  .legal li {
    max-width: 760px;
    color: var(--muted, #a1a1aa);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .legal p {
    margin: 0 0 17px;
  }

  .legal ul {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }

  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: 7px;
  }

  .legal strong {
    color: #e4e4e7;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: #c4b5fd;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .legal a:hover {
    color: #ddd6fe;
  }

  .updated {
    margin-bottom: 32px !important;
    color: #71717a !important;
    font-size: .82rem;
  }

  .notice {
    margin-top: 48px !important;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.025);
    font-size: .88rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal {
      padding-top: 45px;
      padding-bottom: 70px;
    }

    .legal h2 {
      margin-top: 34px;
    }
  }
</style>
